<title>USA: Yurie Systems says shares to be released.</title>
<headline>Yurie Systems says shares to be released.</headline>
<dateline>LANDOVER, Md. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yurie Systems Inc said on Friday that Alex, Brown &amp; Sons Inc agreed to release 10 percent of roughly 20.6 million shares held by directors, officers and shareholders.</p>
<p>The shares to be released are subject to lock-up agreements due to expire on August 4, the company said in a statement. The release, which will be effective on May 30, allows shareholders to sell a portion of their holdings on the open market before the lock-up expires.</p>
<p>Yurie conducted an intial public offering in February at $12 a share.</p>
</text>
